After Apple <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/airpods-5-announced-improved-anc/">introduced the AirPods 5 last week</a>, we got a set to take home and review. We've been testing the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods/">AirPods 5</a> for the last week and have some initial thoughts.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="AirPods 5 Mini Review: Buy These Over the Pros for &#36;149?" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/LvO7uC89G5U" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe><em><a href="https://www.youtube.com/user/macrumors?sub_confirmation=1">Subscribe to the MacRumors YouTube channel</a> for more videos.</em></div><br/>
The &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; have the same overall design and fit as the AirPods 4, so they're just as comfortable as the prior-generation model.<br/>
<br/>
Active Noise Cancellation has been improved through new internal acoustic architecture, and it's surprisingly good. The &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; don't have silicone ear tips so you might not expect ANC to work as well as earbuds with a tighter fit, but there is a noticeable improvement over the ANC version of the AirPods 4.<br/>
<br/>
Apple says the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; use low-noise microphones and a new compressor tuned for open-ear ANC. The compressor is tuned to a wider frequency range and can react faster than before when conditions change. Sound is measured for the left and right ears independently, correcting for fit leaks to further improve ANC.<br/>
<br/>
Sound quality on the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; was muddier than on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/airpods-pro/">AirPods Pro 3</a>, especially in the low mids. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> has custom EQ, though, which allows for adjustments. The &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; support Adaptive Audio and Transparency, so they have most of the same audio features as the &zwnj;AirPods Pro 3&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
Apple used to limit ANC to the higher-end version of the AirPods 4, but with the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj;, it's universal. You can now get AirPods with ANC for just &#36;129. There's an upgraded model with a Wireless Charging Case, an extra hour of battery life, and swipe-based controls on the stem for &#36;149. The base model has four hours of battery with ANC, while the upgraded version offers five hours.<br/>
<br/>
Live Translation, Adaptive Audio, Conversation Awareness, and other features that were previously limited to the higher-end AirPods 4 model are now on all models. Dust and water resistance has improved, and the AirPods have an IP57 rating, so they'll hold up better to sweat and moisture exposure.<br/>
<br/>
With the ANC upgrade and the price drop, the &zwnj;AirPods 5&zwnj; are an excellent value. If you've been hesitant to get AirPods because of the price, this is the version to get. People who have AirPods Pro or AirPods 4 with ANC don't need to upgrade, but it's a big improvement if you have older AirPods.<br/>
